{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825103052,"sessionID":"ses_f46297742ffe9mtUSz9GNRYMps","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e3b078001Qrfzio1mkyscIw","sessionID":"ses_f46297742ffe9mtUSz9GNRYMps","messageID":"msg_0b9e39781001cLLARj9m0e2ciL","type":"tool","id":"call_00_YCES4HP2rhwaaHVDB8y62681","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/macgray && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport openpyxl\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/mac-gray.xlsx')\nws = wb['Questions']\nfor r in range(2, ws.max_row+1):\n    print('====', ws.cell(row=r,column=1).value, '|', ws.cell(row=r,column=2).value)\n    for c in (3,4,5,6):\n        print('   ', ws.cell(row=r,column=c).value[:220] if ws.cell(row=r,column=c).value else '')\n    print('    Status:', ws.cell(row=r,column=7).value)\nws2 = wb['Deal ledger']\nprint('\\n--- sample row R019 (inferred residual) ---')\nfor r in range(2, ws2.max_row+1):\n    if ws2.cell(row=r,column=15).value=='R019':\n        hdr=[ws2.cell(row=1,column=c).value for c in range(1,40)]\n        for c in range(1,40):\n            v=ws2.cell(row=r,column=c).value\n            if v not in (None,''): print(hdr[c-1], '::', str(v)[:300])\n        break\nEOF"},"output":"==== Q1 | Process segmentation and round map\n    Accept one process (Process 1) and the four-round map. R1 anchor = 06/24/2013 sale decision (rejected candidates: 10/23/2012 engagement R002, 04/08/2013 contact R004, 06/21/2013 proposal R008; first outreach wave undated\n    R1 anchor and 50-party outreach: P-022, P-023, P-024; R2: P-037, P-038; R3: P-055; R4: P-061, P-062; context P-002. Working dates and finality as recorded on rows R001, R010, R023, R033, R040.\n    R001, R002, R004, R007, R008, R010, R023, R033, R040 (Process, Round, Round finality, Due date)\n    Renumbers rounds and moves bid/outcome rows and tallies; Summary round map changes. No facts change.\n    Status: Pending\n==== Q2 | Deadlines and their treatment\n    Accept: 07/23/2013 (preliminary IOIs) = Late bids accepted (Party B and Party C submitted 07/24 and were reviewed 07/25); 09/09/2013 (revised written proposals) = Late bids accepted (Party A and Party C submitted 09/10 a\n    Due dates: P-025; late submissions and review: P-035, P-036, P-052, P-054; final due date and next step: P-055, P-058, P-061; exclusivity extension: P-077, P-081.\n    R017, R026, R027, R034, R042, R048 (Deadline treatment, Due date)\n    Treatment labels only; no price or participation changes. If the 09/18 round were read as unclear, Enforced would fall back to Unclear.\n    Status: Pending\n==== Q3 | NDA population, residual cohorts and the auction screen\n    Accept the representation: 20 confidentiality signers = 4 individually recorded (Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) + 16 residual financial signers; 16 residual non-submitters at 07/23/2013. Base caveat: the filing\n    20 signers and composition P-025; four bidders P-036, P-038; \"other potential bidders\" (Reasons) X-018.\n    R011, R019, R012–R016, R018–R021, R025, R046 (Count, Type, Outcome basis)\n    Changes residual counts and the non-submitter cohort; screening conclusion (met) is unchanged on any reading with at least two independent signers.\n    Status: Pending\n==== Q4 | Inferred participation outcomes (closing rows)\n    Accept: Party A and Party B Dropped by target on 09/24/2013 (Inferred: exclusivity; Decided by Target; Exit reason Not stated; no notice inferred) and the 16 residual signers Did not submit at 07/23/2013 (Inferred: resid\n    Exclusivity execution P-067; live rival bids P-058; base and accounting P-025, P-036, P-038.\n    R019, R038, R043, R044 (Outcome basis, Decided by, Exit reason, Count)\n    If a named exit for an anonymous signer were later established, it would be an identity mapping only — no counts move; if Party C’s silence were read as withdrawal, relabel Withdrew (agency still unknown).\n    Status: Pending\n==== Q5 | Formality of final-round indications\n    Accept Formal for the 09/18/2013 final-round rows (CSC/Pamplona R035, Party B R037, Party A reaffirmation R036) as responses on the requested basis to a genuine final solicitation; earlier indications remain Informal; no\n    Final request and responses P-055, P-058; winner reaches agreement P-061, P-062, P-066, P-067.\n    R028–R031 (Informal), R035–R037 (Formal), R041 (carried Formal), R008, R018–R021 (Informal)\n    If all stay Informal, the winner has no Formal row and the deal reads as an informal-only process; bidding counts and prices do not change.\n    Status: Pending\n==== Q6 | Conditions levels (diligence-period and financing readings)\n    Accept: CSC/Pamplona 09/09, 09/18 and 09/21 rows = Light (committed financing; the two-week exclusive negotiation is treated as an exclusivity request, not an attached substantive diligence period); Party A and Party B r\n    Financing statements P-051, P-052; exclusivity requests P-051, P-058, P-062; certainty assessment P-061; pre-diligence context P-034, P-035; diligence period P-046, P-068.\n    R008, R018–R021, R028–R031, R035–R037, R041 (Conditions level, Conditions detail)\n    Reading the two-week exclusivity as an attached diligence period would move CSC/Pamplona’s last rows to Heavy and change the buyer-commitment profile presented in Summary.\n    Status: Pending\n==== Q7 | Prices, package values and consideration comparability\n    Accept: Party B’s 09/18/2013 row carries the bidder-stated package value $21.50 in the price cells with Price origin Stated, All cash = No, Cash at closing $19.00, and the $2.50 option value and five-year vesting in Term\n    Party B package P-058; ranges P-019, P-035, P-039, P-052; $21.25 P-062, P-064; comparability X-006, X-011.\n    R037, R035, R036, R028–R031, R018–R021, R008 (Price low/high, Price kind, Price origin, All cash, Cash at closing)\n    Changes how Party B’s nominal $21.50 package compares with CSC/Pamplona’s $21.25 cash; no ranking change is asserted by the ledger.\n    