{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825125160,"sessionID":"ses_f46297742ffe9mtUSz9GNRYMps","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e3e95b0010C4bNPUDf7S0S6_text-0","sessionID":"ses_f46297742ffe9mtUSz9GNRYMps","messageID":"msg_0b9e3e95b0010C4bNPUDf7S0S6","type":"text","text":"The workbook is complete and validated. Here's the delivery.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n**`/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/mac-gray.xlsx`** — four visible sheets (**Deal ledger**, **Summary**, **Questions**, **Source text**) plus a hidden **Lists** sheet for the drop-downs. 50 ledger rows, 87 background paragraphs (P-001–P-087) and 42 other used passages (X-001–X-042) in Source text, with working local links from every ledger row.\n\n## The sale, in brief\n\nMac-Gray's Board kept a standing strategic review; after CSC was sold to Pamplona (May 2013), the Board authorized exploration (04/05/2013), Mac-Gray's banker approached Party A (04/08/2013), and Party A made an unsolicited $17–19 all-cash proposal (06/21/2013). On 06/24/2013 the Board formed a six-member Special Committee, excluded CEO MacDonald and Moab's Rothenberg for rollover conflicts, and launched a solicitation of 50 parties (15 strategic, 35 financial). Twenty signed confidentiality agreements (2 strategic, 18 financial; four individually recorded, 16 as a residual cohort) and four bidders advanced through staged diligence: **CSC/Pamplona** ($18.50 → 19.50 → 20.75 → 21.25), **Party B** ($17–18 → 18.50 → a $21.50-valued package that was mostly contingent options), **Party A** ($17–19 → 18–19, best and final) and **Party C** ($15–17 → 16–17, dropped out at the final deadline). Mac-Gray granted CSC/Pamplona exclusivity on 09/24/2013, extended it to 10/15/2013 after resolving the termination-fee dispute, and signed the all-cash $21.25 merger on 10/14/2013, announced 10/15/2013. The proxy reports no closing by its 12/04/2013 date (special meeting 01/08/2014; closing expected January 2014; no go-shop and no post-signing competing proposal disclosed).\n\n## Most consequential review items (recommendations)\n\n1. **Round map (Q1)** — Recommend the four-round map: R1 06/24/2013 (launch, anchor decision), R2 07/25/2013 (four advancing, staged disclosure), R3 09/11/2013 (final indications, *Announced as final*), R4 09/21/2013 (exclusive definitive negotiation, *Inferred final*); 2011-2012 Discussions kept as reverse-direction context. Alternatives (08/27 letter, 09/19, 09/24) are retained as their own rows.\n2. **Deadlines (Q2)** — 07/23 and 09/09 = *Late bids accepted* (Party B/C submitted 07/24; Party A/C 09/10, all reviewed); 09/18 = *Enforced* (selection/exclusivity the next day, nothing accepted late). Exclusivity expiry is tracked in Terms, not as a bid deadline.\n3. **Residual cohorts (Q3)** — 16 financial NDA signers and 16 non-submitters are inferences from the stated 20-signer base minus the four accounted bidders; the filing's \"other potential bidders\" phrasing is the main caveat. Auction screen: **met**.\n4. **Inferred closes (Q4)** — Party A and Party B Dropped by target 09/24/2013 (Inferred: exclusivity); Party C's 09/18 non-submission is stated (no reasons given → Unknown/Not stated).\n5. **Formality (Q5)** — Final-round indications classified Formal (responses to the final solicitation), earlier ones Informal; no returned markups anywhere, and the winner therefore has a Formal row before signing.\n6. **Conditions (Q6)** — CSC/Pamplona Light (committed financing; the two-week exclusive negotiation read as exclusivity, not an attached diligence period — the borderline call flagged); Party A/B Heavy (no firm financing commitment).\n7. **Party B's package (Q7)** — Price cells carry the bidder-stated $21.50 with Cash at closing $19.00 and All cash = No; the $2.50 option value and five-year vesting sit in Terms.\n8. **Date conventions (Q8)** — Including the 2011-2012 window midpoint, \"by\"-bounded rows, and the source typo \"July 27, 2103\" read as 07/27/2013.\n\n## What I could not verify / limitations\n\n- **Excel rendering**: LibreOffice crashed in this environment, so I could not do a live render/print check. Row heights are estimated so wrapped text displays fully; formulas are real SUMIFS with `fullCalcOnLoad` set, and I verified their results by evaluating them against the ledger data (20 / 2 / 4 / 4 / 3 / 1 / 17 / 2) — but Excel itself has not recalculated them here.\n- **Links**: internal hyperlinks were written and inspected in the file XML; I could not click-test them in Excel.\n- **Page numbers**: derived from the filing's composition pagination and spot-checked against the table of contents (background 27–41, costs sections 42/45/52/54/58/60); not verified for every paragraph.\n- **Quotes**: all ledger quotations were programmatically matched against the Source text sheet (whitespace/punctuation-normalized), but that checks recoverability, not interpretation.\n- **Column groups**: the expandable field groups are collapsed outline groups; the field headers themselves label each group (no separate group-label rows, consistent with \"no merged data cells\").\n\nNo workbook features beyond the specified sheets, tables, drop-downs, links and formulas were added; no other scope, currency or CVR issues arose.","time":{"start":1789825116519,"end":1789825125160}}}
